# DTF tier manifest: pacman-hosted  (artifact-keeper#3343, #4424; both shipped
# in 1.11.0)
# Profile-set: filesystem + the real pacman client (client.pacman: the
# official archlinux image idling on the DTF network). Packages are built in
# that container with bsdtar in makepkg's layout (.MTREE, .PKGINFO, files) and
# signed with a throwaway gpg key; pacman is pointed at a pacman.conf naming
# ONLY the AK repository, so no Arch mirror is contacted. Nothing is installed
# on the host or in the image.
#
# THE BEHAVIOUR
# #3343  A `pacman` repository accepts .pkg.tar.* uploads under
#        /pacman/{repo}/ (filename checked against .PKGINFO; re-upload 409),
#        renders {section}.db and {section}.files on demand for any section
#        name, embeds an uploaded .sig as %PGPSIG%, serves a detached
#        .db.sig when a gpg signing key is attached (404 otherwise), and
#        deletes with DELETE /pacman/{repo}/{arch}/{package}.
# #4424  .files is cached per repository package set; a publish or delete is
#        picked up on the next request.
#
# THE GATES
#   (FIX)      RED on 1.10.0 (no pacman format: create fails, every route
#              404), GREEN on 1.11.0 and main:
#              #3343 upload 201, .sig 201, misnamed 400, duplicate 409.
#              #3343 dtfp.db lists dtf-hello and dtf-tool; dtf-hello's desc
#                    carries %FILENAME%, the package's %SHA256SUM% and the
#                    uploaded signature as %PGPSIG%.
#              #3343 pacman -Syy / -S dtf-hello installs its file; pacman -Fyy;
#                    pacman -F attributes a file to dtfp/dtf-tool; -Fl lists.
#              #4424 publish dtf-extra -> pacman -Fl dtf-extra lists its file;
#                    DELETE -> 204, then -Fl finds nothing and the .db no
#                    longer lists it while dtf-hello stays.
#              #3343 with a signing key attached (POST /api/v1/signing/keys
#                    key_type gpg + /signing/repositories/{uuid}/config):
#                    dtfs.db.sig is GOODSIG against /pacman/{repo}/gpg-key.asc;
#                    with both keys lsigned in pacman's keyring, SigLevel =
#                    Required installs dtf-tool; the same policy refuses the
#                    unsigned repository (its .db.sig is 404).
#   (CONTROL)  must hold on BOTH images: the fixture is a valid package
#              (pacman -Qip, pacman -U installs and -R removes it from the
#              file), and the client container reaches the backend. A red
#              below is then the server's.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: a few dozen requests back to back.
PROFILES="storage.filesystem client.pacman"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
